WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:07.240
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week’s
Doctor Who Episode Mummy on the Orient Express

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.999
brought back a famous british comedian, featured
pop star Foxes and explained the Clara situation.

00:00:11.999 --> 00:00:17.210
The way things ended was very controversial
but we can talk about that as we dig through

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.210
everything.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.520
Just a reminder, the giveaway is regenerating
again this week.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.630
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.350
Starting with Top 5 Moments.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.560
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.360
I’ll wait just a sec...here we go.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.250
Number 5 - Foxes Is a Traincar Lounge Singer

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:39.420
I’m not a huge Foxes fan or anything, but
I love that she was singing Freddy Mercury.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.780
It was Queen’s “Don’t Stop Me Now”
to be precise, very appropriate for a story

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.090
set on a train.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:50.170
There have been a lot of famous people guest
starring on Doctor Who this year.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:55.219
I don’t mind seeing familiar faces as long
as they don’t derail the story.

00:00:55.219 --> 00:01:05.320
Foxes turned out to 
be one of the holograms, so she vanished part

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.320
of the way through the episode.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.040
So if you didn’t like her you only had to
deal with it for a little bit.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.350
Number 4 - Frank Skinner is the Chief Engineer

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:15.140
This was a bit of a twist, in real life, for
anyone who doesn’t know, Skinner is a Comedian.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:20.280
But he wasn’t playing an overtly comedic
role in the episode.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.780
If you watched the Five-ish Doctors Special
during the 50th Anniversary, he also had a

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.500
cameo in that as a Dalek Operator.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.439
I really like it when comedians are given
the chance to do something more dramatic.

00:01:30.439 --> 00:01:39.090
Everyone needs to watch Eddie Izzard on Hannibal
Season 1 if you haven’t seen it yet.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:42.159
Comedians are inherently dark people, so that
might be why they’re so good at playing

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:44.090
dramatic characters.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:48.479
Skinner’s first run in with The Doctor was
probably one of the funniest moments in the

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:49.479
episode.

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:54.299
He did seem like a match for wits and he even
knew how to repair the TARDIS.

00:01:54.299 --> 00:02:06.700
I feel like that bit with him at the end,
talking about how to fix things, raised more

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.789
questions than it answered.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:14.510
And the bit about The Doctor offering him
a spot on board as a companion seemed more

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:19.270
like a conceit of the whole Clara plot.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:32.970
I know a lot of you guys want to see another
male companion, I even though Danny Pink was

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:37.840
going to be one until the whole Clara Romance
thing was explained.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.890
Let me know though, if we did get a male companion,
would you care how old he is.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:46.099
Like would you rather it be someone younger
like Danny Pink or do you not care.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.040
Number 3 - The Doctor Lies

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:52.700
Does anyone else feel like The Doctor was
off his rocker a little?

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:57.110
Lying is a totally normal thing to be expected,
but the whole bit with Clara and trying to

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.900
get the next woman to die was extreme.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:05.470
I loved that line, I don’t care what you
tell her, just lie and tell her I’ll save

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:06.470
her.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.989
Anything to get her here.

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:14.489
Even though he messed with her head and took
her place it didn’t seem completely geniune.

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:17.590
It was like he only did that to make Clara
calm down.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.230
His explanation at the end wasn’t much comfort
either, it was like he was telling Clara that

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:24.769
she should just believe what she thinks will
make her happiest.

00:03:24.769 --> 00:03:28.200
It’s like he’s dodging the question about
whether or not he’s a good person.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.510
It’s a bit of a cop out on his part and
I think things like that will haunt him during

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:33.900
the finale.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.790
Number 2 - The Mummy is an Ancient Soldier

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:41.710
I liked the are you my mummy and gasmask callback
to Empty Child.

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:46.030
The solution to the problem was kind of rushed
in the end, but there was the whole conceit

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.030
of 66 seconds.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:51.519
So I’ll give that a pass.

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:58.209
But now I’m wondering what War that soldier
was a part of.

00:03:58.209 --> 00:04:03.150
It was tied to the scroll or flag or however
you want to think about it, but the only reason

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:08.409
it continued to drain energy from people was
because the regenerative device inside it

00:04:08.409 --> 00:04:09.409
was malfunctioning.

00:04:09.409 --> 00:04:14.200
I think it’s an interesting metaphor for
the Doctor, the soldier, clearly a monster,

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.579
just like the Doctor was for most of the episode,
wanted to die but could not.

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:18.579
He was forced to keep regenerating himself
on the energy of other people.

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:21.690
It’s almost like they were saying The Doctor
has been sucking the life out of Clara to

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:22.800
keep himself going.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:28.160
That’s not the case, but I feel like it’s
in the subtext.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.990
In reality, what I think is going on is they’re
foreshadowing the finale.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:34.190
There have been liberal spoilers for what
goes on.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:38.390
So please use spoiler tags if you know what
I’m talking about.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:43.740
But see if you can connect these things: Dead
Soldiers unable to stop, forced to keep fighting.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:49.280
And which other new character on the show
is everyone calling “The Soldier?”

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.009
Again, please use spoiler tags.

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:56.300
and my Number 1 WTF Moment - Clara Changes
Her Mind

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:01.389
So this isn’t my number 1 because it’s
awesome, it’s because it’s a major holy

00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:02.389
crap.

00:05:02.389 --> 00:05:05.520
I actually don’t think this is a hopeful
thing.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.990
Something about the whole scene feels ominous.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:12.110
Like Clara should have learned her lesson,
by going against Danny’s better judgement,

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:15.110
she’ll get smacked in the face with a terrible
situation.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:20.970
It’s almost like she wasn’t listening
to The Doctor when she woke up on that planet.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:26.430
He was telling her he was saving her and those
other people just happened to come along.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:36.190
He wasn’t purposefully going to let them
die, but if 

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:55.700
they had, he wouldn’t have cared that much.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:59.270
Let me know what you favorite moment was,
and do you think Clara made the right choice.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:00.630
I totally think this was a bad thing.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.330
It’s gone from this place of carefree adventure
into darkness.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.340
That’s one of the major arcs of the season,
heading into darkness.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.310
Overall I gave the episode a B, I loved the
story concept.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:10.891
An ancient soldier forced to continue fighting
a war that ended thousands of years ago, masquerading

00:06:10.891 --> 00:06:11.891
on a mummy on one of the most famous passenger
trains in history.

00:06:11.891 --> 00:06:15.650
The original Orient Express ran during the
late Victorian Era, which is why it looked

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.069
like they were back in victorian times.

00:06:17.069 --> 00:06:20.040
I’m wondering if there’s any special significance
to them constantly re-visiting that period

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.040
in series 8.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:25.680
They started the season there, Missy, the
main villain this year is dressed in a victorian

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:30.139
manner, it might just be that the producers
and set designers think that the period is

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:31.560
interesting from a story telling perspective.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:32.560
I did like Clara and the Doctor’s outfits.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.990
I mean I do enjoy the visual style of the
victorian era.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.920
I did think it was a bit of a downer when
they took it all back halfway through the

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:39.319
episode when they revealed it was a futuristic
lab.

00:06:39.319 --> 00:06:42.980
I would have just liked the idea of a normal
starliner designed to look like the Orient

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:43.980
Express.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:47.729
I don’t know why they needed the added evil
scientist aspect, unless it was meant to be

00:06:47.729 --> 00:06:51.080
something that will tie in with the finale.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.880
We are down to the final 3 episodes.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:56.289
I’m counting the last two as a two parter,
even though I think the Christmas Special

00:06:56.289 --> 00:07:00.479
will address things from the finale.

00:07:00.479 --> 00:07:16.360
Danny Pink has a big role in next week’s
episode, so I’m interested to see if we’ll

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.660
see any crazy twists with his character.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.440
I will be doing a Q&amp;A for this tomorrow.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:26.050
Walking Dead is starting tomorrow night too.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:34.930
Everyone in the UK will be able to watch it
within about 8 hours of people in the United

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:35.930
States.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:36.930
So everyone check it out.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:41.110
Right now click here for the Q&amp;A, I’ll update
the annotation as soon as I post it and click

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:42.690
here for my episode 7 video.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.639
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and I’ll see you tomorrow!

